  "limitations": [
    "Fixtures are small (one module plus tests); the evaluation measures the delegation protocol, not coding quality at scale.",
    "The requirements checklist is shown to executors, so some items can be satisfied from the checklist itself; qualitative self-reports carry the instruction-side signal.",
    "All runs used one machine, one user Codex config (workspace-write, on-request, automatic reviewer), one model (gpt-6-luna), and ChatGPT login; API-key auth, Linux, and WSL were not exercised.",
    "Executors ran as subagents of the parent session; parallel scenarios shared the machine, and one executor's process check once matched another scenario's run (iter1-A).",
    "Holdout H was used once as a true holdout (iter9) and again as a regression check (iter10) after the helper gained reap.",
    "Unclear points were counted by the parent after removing duplicates and executor-attributed shell mistakes; counts are approximate."
  ]
